{
  "ai": {
    "chunks": [
      "The eminent Shaykh Abu Ja'far Muhammad b. Ali b. al-Husayn b. Musa b. Babawayh al-Qummi (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated to us, saying: Muhammad b. Musa b. al-Mutawakkil (may Allah have mercy on him) narrated to us, saying: Abdullah b. Ja'far al-Himyari narrated to us, from Muhammad b. al-Husayn b. Abi al-Khattab, from Ali b. Asbat, from Ali b. Abi Hamza, from Abu Basir, from Abu Abdullah al-Sadiq Ja'far b. Muhammad (peace be upon him), who said: Among that which Allah, Blessed and Exalted, admonished Isa son of Maryam (peace be upon him) was that He said to him:",
      "O Isa, adorn yourself with the adornment of religion, which is the love of the poor, and walk upon the earth with humility, and pray upon the places of prostration, and perform ablution with water wherever you find it. O Isa, I am your Lord and the Lord of your forefathers. My name is One. I am the One, the Self-Subsisting, Creator of all things. All things are My creation, and to Me they shall return. O Isa, you are My servant and son of My maidservant. I nurtured you for Myself. I created you for the worship of My servants, that they may turn to you in what concerns them of My affair. Do not diminish from what I have conveyed to you.",
      "Remember Me in yourself and I shall remember you in Myself. Remember Me in a gathering and I shall remember you in a gathering better than the gathering of humans. So seek help from Me, not from My creation. O Isa, wake in the night seeking My pleasure, and make yourself thirsty during your day for the day of your need. O Isa, fear Me and make My servants fear Me, so that perhaps the sinners may refrain from what they engage in, and not be disobedient except knowingly.",
      "O Isa, the world is but a prison and what is beautiful in it is ugly. For the son of Adam it is nothing but a test. You are My servant and the world has no permanence for you, so be content with what I have apportioned for you. O Isa, be compassionate and merciful, and be as you wish others to be towards you. Do what you wish others to do unto you, and think often of death and the departure from this world. O Isa, do not hesitate in fleeing from that which is hateful, for what is hateful passes not without leaving its mark upon you.",
      "O Isa, sustain yourself with rough bread and greenery, and leave what is excess. Know what goes out from your mouth. Be content with a little of the world's goods with a sound religion, for you are sufficient. O Isa, what comes to you of trials from Me, accept it with patience. O Isa, you are answerable, so be merciful to the weak as I am merciful to you. O Isa, have I not been most gracious to you? Have I not blessed you among creation? O Isa, guard your tongue and look at your deeds as a sinful servant looks, not as a lord looks at others.",
      "O Isa, make your heart merciful to the weak, and your eyes tearful, and your skin fearful. Remember the life to come and what is before you of death. Do not take the covenant of Allah lightly, for I have cursed the one who breaks it. O Isa, whatever wrong is done to you, do not repay it to others. If someone strikes your right cheek, offer the left. Draw near to Me with love and turn away from the ignorant. O Isa, say to the oppressors of Bani Israel: Wisdom weeps in fear of Me while you babble with laughter! Has My absolution reached you, or do you have immunity from My punishment? Or do you expose yourselves to My retribution? By Me I swear, I shall make you an example for those who come after.",
      "Then I commend to you — O son of Maryam the virgin, the chaste — the master of the Messengers and My beloved among them, Ahmad, possessor of the red camel and the radiant face luminous with light, the pure of heart, the strong in courage, the modest and the generous. For he is a mercy for all worlds and the master of the children of Adam in My sight. On the Day he meets Me, he will be the most honored of the forerunners to Me and the closest of the Messengers to Me — the Arab, the unlettered, the judge by My religion, the patient in My cause, the one who strives against the polytheists with his body for My religion.",
      "O Isa, I command you to inform the Children of Israel about him, and to command them to believe in him, have faith in him, follow him, and support him. Isa said: My Lord, who is he? He said: O Isa, accept him, and for you is My pleasure. He said: O Allah, I accept. Who is he? He said: Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah",
      "to all of mankind. He is the closest of them to Me in station and the most worthy of My intercession. Blessed is he as a prophet, and blessed is his community if they meet Me upon his path. The people of the earth praise him and the people of heaven seek forgiveness for him. Trustworthy, blessed, purified — the best of those who passed and those who remain in My sight. He will come in the last of times. When he appears, the sky will pour its rain and the earth will bring forth its blossoms, and I will bless whatever he places his hand upon. He has many wives and few children. He resides in Bakka, the place of Ibrahim's foundation. O Isa, his religion is the pure monotheism and his qibla is from Makka. He is of My party and I am with him — blessed is he! For him is al-Kawthar and the greatest station in the Gardens of Eden. He will live the noblest life and be taken as a martyr. He has a pool stretching from Makka to the rising of the sun, of sealed pure wine, with vessels like the stars of the sky, its water sweet, containing every drink and the taste of every fruit in Paradise. Whoever drinks from it a sip shall never thirst again. I will send him in an interval between you and him. His secret matches his outward, and his word matches his deed. He does not command the people except with what he himself practices first. His religion is struggle in hardship and ease. The lands submit to him. The ruler of Rome will submit to him, upon his religion and the religion of his father Ibrahim. He names Allah at meals and spreads the greeting of peace. He prays while people sleep. He has five consecutive daily prayers. He opens with the takbir and concludes with the taslim. He aligns his feet in prayer as the angels align their feet. His heart is humble before Me. Light is in his chest, truth is on his tongue, and he is with the truth wherever it may be. His eyes sleep but his heart does not. For him is the intercession. Upon his community the Hour will come. My hand is above their hands when they pledge allegiance to him. Whoever breaks his pledge, he only harms himself. Whoever fulfills it, I will fulfill My promise to him with Paradise. So command the oppressors of Bani Israel not to efface his books, nor distort his practice, and to convey greetings of peace to him, for he has a great status in My station.",
      "O Isa, everything that draws you near to Me, I have already guided you to it, and everything that distances you from Me, I have forbidden you from it. So seek for yourself. O Isa, indeed the world is sweet, and I have only employed you in it to obey Me. So avoid from it what I have warned you about, and take from it freely what I have given you. Look at your deeds as a sinful, erring servant looks, and do not look at the deeds of others as a lord looks. Be ascetic in it and do not desire it lest you perish. O Isa, reflect and ponder, and look at the regions of the earth — how was the end of the oppressors. O Isa, all My counsel is advice for you, and all My words are truth, and I am the Manifest Truth. Truly I say: if you disobey Me after I have informed you, you shall have no protector or helper besides Me. O Isa, humble your heart with awe and look at those who are lower than you, and do not look at those above you. Know that the root of every sin and transgression is the love of the world, so do not love it, for I do not love it. O Isa, purify your heart through Me and increase your remembrance of Me in solitude. Know that My delight is that you humble yourself before Me — be in that alive and not dead. O Isa, do not associate anything with Me and be on guard from Me. Do not be deluded by health, and do not envy yourself, for the world is like a passing shadow — what comes from it is like what departs. So compete in good deeds with your utmost, and be with the truth wherever it may be, even if you are cut and burned by fire. Do not disbelieve in Me after knowing Me, and do not be among the ignorant. O Isa, pour tears from your eyes for Me and humble your heart to Me. O Isa, seek My forgiveness in times of hardship, for I rescue the distressed and answer the desperate, and I am the Most Merciful of the merciful."
    ],
