    "seo_question": "What did Allah advise Prophet Isa (Jesus) about worship, asceticism, and Prophet Muhammad?",
    "summary": "The eminent Shaykh Abu Ja'far Muhammad b. Ali b. al-Husayn b. Musa b. Babawayh al-Qummi narrated to us, from a chain of narrators reaching Imam al-Sadiq (peace be upon him), who said: Among that which Allah, Blessed and Exalted, admonished Isa son of Maryam (peace be upon him) was that He said: O Isa, adorn yourself with the religion through love of the poor and walk on the earth with humility. I am your Lord and Creator of all things. You are My servant, so remember Me and seek My help alone. Wake at night seeking My pleasure. Fear Me and teach My servants to fear Me. The world is but a prison — be content with what I have apportioned you. Be compassionate and merciful. Whatever wrong is done to you, do not repay it — offer the other cheek. Sustain yourself with rough bread and greenery. Guard your tongue. Look at your deeds humbly. I commend to you the master of the Messengers, Ahmad — a mercy to the worlds, the Arab, the unlettered, the patient in My cause. His religion is pure monotheism, his qibla from Makka. He prays five daily prayers, his secret matches his outward. For him is al-Kawthar and intercession. Command Bani Israel to believe in him. Everything that draws you near to Me I have guided you to. The world is sweet but fleeting. Compete in good deeds. Humble your heart, pour tears for Me, and seek My forgiveness in hardship — for I rescue the distressed and answer the desperate, and I am the Most Merciful of the merciful.",
